answer.worked:
Applying the sine rule to $\Delta OBC$ and $\Delta OCA$ in a similar way:
In $\Delta OBC$, $\angle OCB = \gamma - \theta$:
$$\begin{align*}
\frac{OB}{\sin(\gamma - \theta)} &= \frac{OC}{\sin\theta} \implies \frac{OB}{OC} = \frac{\sin(\gamma - \theta)}{\sin\theta}
\end{align*}$$
In $\Delta OCA$, $\angle OAC = \alpha - \theta$:
$$\begin{align*}
\frac{OC}{\sin(\alpha - \theta)} &= \frac{OA}{\sin\theta} \implies \frac{OC}{OA} = \frac{\sin(\alpha - \theta)}{\sin\theta}
\end{align*}$$
Multiplying the three ratios together yields $1$:
$$\begin{align*}
\frac{OA}{OB} \times \frac{OB}{OC} \times \frac{OC}{OA} &= \frac{\sin(\beta - \theta)}{\sin\theta} \times \frac{\sin(\gamma - \theta)}{\sin\theta} \times \frac{\sin(\alpha - \theta)}{\sin\theta} \\
1 &= \frac{\sin(\beta - \theta)\sin(\gamma - \theta)\sin(\alpha - \theta)}{\sin^3\theta} \\
\sin^3\theta &= \sin(\alpha - \theta)\sin(\beta - \theta)\sin(\gamma - \theta)
\end{align*}$$

Write the cotangent functions in terms of sine and cosine:
$$\begin{align*}
\cot x - \cot y &= \frac{\cos x}{\sin x} - \frac{\cos y}{\sin y} \\
&= \frac{\cos x \sin y - \sin x \cos y}{\sin x \sin y}
\end{align*}$$
Using the sine compound angle identity in the numerator:
$$\begin{align*}
\cot x - \cot y &= \frac{\sin(y - x)}{\sin x \sin y}
\end{align*}$$

Using the identity from part (c), substitute $x = \theta$ and $y = \alpha$, $\beta$, $\gamma$ respectively:
$$\begin{align*}
\cot\theta - \cot\alpha &= \frac{\sin(\alpha - \theta)}{\sin\theta \sin\alpha} \\
\cot\theta - \cot\beta &= \frac{\sin(\beta - \theta)}{\sin\theta \sin\beta} \\
\cot\theta - \cot\gamma &= \frac{\sin(\gamma - \theta)}{\sin\theta \sin\gamma}
\end{align*}$$
Multiplying these three expressions:
$$\begin{align*}
(\cot\theta - \cot\alpha)(\cot\theta - \cot\beta)(\cot\theta - \cot\gamma) &= \frac{\sin(\alpha - \theta)\sin(\beta - \theta)\sin(\gamma - \theta)}{\sin^3\theta \sin\alpha \sin\beta \sin\gamma}
\end{align*}$$
Substitute the result from part (b) into the numerator:
$$\begin{align*}
(\cot\theta - \cot\alpha)(\cot\theta - \cot\beta)(\cot\theta - \cot\gamma) &= \frac{\sin^3\theta}{\sin^3\theta \sin\alpha \sin\beta \sin\gamma} \\
&= \frac{1}{\sin\alpha \sin\beta \sin\gamma} \\
&= \csc\alpha \csc\beta \csc\gamma
\end{align*}$$

